  "notes": "USAGE:\nAlthough the platform formerly known as Twitter was renamed to X, the term ツイート remains widely used in Japanese for posts on that platform. The verb form is ツイートする.\n\nリツイート (retweet) means to share someone else's post. {引用|いんよう}ツイート (quote tweet) means to share with added commentary.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ツイートする: to tweet, to post\n- リツイート: retweet\n- {引用|いんよう}ツイート: quote tweet\n- ツイートが{炎上|えんじょう}する: a tweet catches fire (causes backlash)\n- ツイートを{削除|さくじょ}する: to delete a tweet",
